MovieThumbnailer uses the optional ffmpegthumbnailer executable found by
NSTask's tool lookup. Install ffmpegthumbnailer, enable GWorkspace's
thumbnail display, and browse a movie folder. Missing thumbnails are generated
in the background as file icons are requested. Conversions run one at a time;
failed conversions are retried when the source changes or GWorkspace restarts.
Thumbnails > Make thumbnail(s) remains available for explicit regeneration.
The normal GWorkspace build/install includes
this .thumb bundle; no FFmpeg headers or libraries are needed to build it.

The helper's -m option prefers embedded artwork and falls back to a video
frame. Output preserves aspect ratio and fits the existing 64-pixel thumbnail
size. Missing helpers, failed conversions and conversions exceeding 15 seconds
produce no thumbnail. Temporary output is private to each conversion and is
removed afterward. This bundle adds no codec linkage or libs-gui changes.

Run the integration tests with:
  sh Tests/run.sh
The tests require GNUstep development tools, ffmpeg and ffmpegthumbnailer.
